		DESCRIPTION
		        "For port configured with 10G WAN traffic, 
			A failure is a defect that persists beyond the maximum
			time allocated to the transmission system protection
			mechanisms. When this situation occurs, an RFI is sent
			to the far end and will initiate a path protection
			switch if this function has been provisioned.
			-----------------------------
			omtp12PlusInterfaceNumber:
			1 - CLIENT-1
			-----------------------------
			Values :
			If Alarm is Present - Date and Time Stamp
				    eg:2017-5-18,9:47:20.0,+5:30
			If Alarm is Absent  - 0
			-----------------------------"
               ::= { omtp12PlusAlarmQueryEntry 111 }

        omtp12PlusWan10gMsB2ExcessiveErrorAlarm OBJECT-TYPE
		SYNTAX  DisplayString
		MAX-ACCESS  read-only
		STATUS  current
		DESCRIPTION
		        "For port configured with 10G WAN traffic, 
			B2 SF alarm is generated when Parity errors evaluated 
			by byte B2 of Wan10g frame exceeds the 
			'omtp12PlusWan10gMsB2ExcessiveErrorThreshold' threshold
			-----------------------------
			omtp12PlusInterfaceNumber:
			1 - CLIENT-1
			-----------------------------
			Values :
			If Alarm is Present - Date and Time Stamp
				    eg:2017-5-18,9:47:20.0,+5:30
			If Alarm is Absent  - 0
