        omtp12PlusWan10gLossOfSequenceSynchronisationAlarm OBJECT-TYPE
		SYNTAX  DisplayString
		MAX-ACCESS  read-only
		STATUS  current
		DESCRIPTION
		        "For port configured with 10G WAN traffic, 
			Sequence synchronisation shall be considered to be lost
			and re-synchronisation shall be started if:
			The bit error ratio is ≥ 0.20 during an integration
			interval of 1 second; or
			It can be unambiguously identified that the test
			sequence and the reference sequence are out of phase.
			-----------------------------
			omtp12PlusInterfaceNumber:
			1 - CLIENT-1
			-----------------------------
			Values :
			If Alarm is Present - Date and Time Stamp
				    eg:2017-5-18,9:47:20.0,+5:30
			If Alarm is Absent  - 0
			-----------------------------"
               ::= { omtp12PlusAlarmQueryEntry 114 }
               
